---
import BaseLayout from "../../site/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ArrowIcon from "../../site/components/ArrowIcon.astro";
import "../../site/styles/arrow-study.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="Arrow study — Mourne Made" description="A visual study of directional cues for Mourne Made." hideFooter>
  <main class="arrow-study">
    <div class="shell arrow-study-intro">
      <a class="arrow-study-back" href="/prototypes/mobile-menu-study/">← Mobile menu study</a>
      <p class="home-kicker">Mourne Made · component study</p>
      <h1>How should an action point forward?</h1>
      <p class="arrow-study-lede">Three arrow treatments for links and buttons. The label does the explaining; the cue should add direction without becoming decoration.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="shell arrow-study-grid">
      <article class="arrow-option"><p class="arrow-option-name"><span>A</span> Inline arrow</p><div class="arrow-demo"><a href="#">Open the comparison <ArrowIcon /></a></div><p>Current direction: a light horizontal arrow sits naturally after the label.</p></article>
      <article class="arrow-option"><p class="arrow-option-name"><span>B</span> Strong arrow</p><div class="arrow-demo arrow-demo--strong"><a href="#">Open the comparison <ArrowIcon /></a></div><p>A heavier, slightly larger cue makes the action feel more direct.</p></article>
      <article class="arrow-option"><p class="arrow-option-name"><span>C</span> Chevron</p><div class="arrow-demo arrow-demo--chevron"><a href="#">Open the comparison <span aria-hidden="true">›</span></a></div><p>The quietest option. Typography leads and the chevron only confirms the destination.</p></article>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
